{
  "_note": "Device map for the Clarett 8Pre USB (1235:8208) driven by fcp-server through the kernel's fcp driver. This model does not answer DEVMAP_INFO (0x80000c, FCP error 7), so it cannot describe itself: this file is its description, loaded by fcp_devmap_read_from_file() by USB product id. Paired with fcp-alsa-map-8208.json.",
  "_provenance": "Offsets, widths and commit activates from Focusrite's published device descriptor for this model, cross-checked against the in-kernel scarlett2 driver's config set (scarlett2_config_set_clarett) and router layout (clarett_8pre_info mux_assignment and meter_map). Clean-room: no vendor device map or driver was used.",
  "_limitations": [
    "peak-index is the destination's position in scarlett2's mux_assignment table for the speed band (GET_METER returns one value per table entry, in table order); peak-index-m / -h are the same at double and quad speed, where ADAT and PCM entries drop out and the rest shift down. Per-rate meters need an fcp-server that follows the sample rate; otherwise the 48 kHz layout is used at every rate.",
    "At quad speed the mixer and ADAT outputs are absent from the router table.",
    "masterVolume (the front-panel knob) is read-only; outputs set to HW follow the knob in the device.",
    "notify-client: dim/mute 0x200000 and monitor 0x400000, the descriptor's notification bits.",
    "router-pin is a DECIMAL string because fcp-server parses it with atoi()."
  ],
